Package: latex2grad
Type: Package
Title: Verifiable Differentiation of Formulas Written in LaTeX
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Che", "Cheng", email = "kiki830621@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Differentiates formulas written in LaTeX (or transcribed from an
    image) end to end: a deterministic grammar parses the LaTeX into an R
    expression tree, a canonical normalizer and printer give the tree a
    round-trip LaTeX form, 'DefDiff' computes the gradient, Hessian, or
    Jacobian symbolically, and every result carries a certificate (round-trip
    status plus a seeded random-point comparison against Richardson-extrapolated
    central differences). Sub-terms outside DefDiff's language are named with
    the reason and differentiated numerically. An optional language model is
    used only at the entry (disambiguation and OCR) and every decision it makes
    is recorded in the report's assumptions.
